---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Software | Macro Evidence"
  description="Software built on Macro Evidence's shared macroeconomic-data foundation, led by Macro Data Observatory."
>
  <PageIntro
    kicker="Software"
    title="Software grows from one shared foundation."
    lead="We build our software ecosystem around one shared macroeconomic-data foundation, with Macro Data Observatory (MDO) as its flagship and foundational platform, rather than parallel systems that recreate the same underlying work."
  />

  <section class="section foundation-section">
    <div class="site-container foundation-grid">
      <div class="foundation-copy">
        <span class="eyebrow">Organization and platform</span>
        <h2>
          Macro Evidence provides the direction. MDO carries the technical and
          product depth.
        </h2>
        <p class="section-intro">
          Mission, stewardship, governance, and organization-wide standards
          belong with Macro Evidence. Data models, pipelines, provider
          integrations, catalogue work, APIs, and product interaction belong
          with Macro Data Observatory.
        </p>
      </div>

      <article class="platform-feature">
        <span class="micro-label">Flagship and foundational platform</span>
        <h3>Macro Data Observatory</h3>
        <p>
          Open-source data infrastructure for acquiring, validating,
          structuring, and maintaining macroeconomic data from authoritative
          public sources through engineered, reproducible pipelines.
        </p>
        <div class="platform-status">
          <span>Status</span>
          <strong>Under active development.</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="action-row">
          <a
            class="primary-action"
            href="https://github.com/macro-evidence/macro-data-observatory"
          >
            Open MDO on GitHub
          </a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="site-container">
      <div class="section-lead-grid">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">A deliberate boundary</span>
          <h2>Shared infrastructure should compound rather than fragment.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="reading">
          <p class="section-intro">
            Future Macro Evidence interfaces and products are intended to
            expose, extend, or operate on the shared foundation instead of
            rebuilding equivalent infrastructure in parallel. That keeps product
            growth compatible with one maintainable core.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card-grid boundary-grid mt-3">
        <article class="identity-panel">
          <h3>Organization</h3>
          <p>
            Macro Evidence owns institutional direction, public governance,
            standards, stewardship, and the broader software portfolio.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="identity-panel">
          <h3>Platform</h3>
          <p>
            MDO owns the technical and product depth of the shared
            macroeconomic-data foundation.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="identity-panel">
          <h3>Future growth</h3>
          <p>
            New interfaces and products should build on that foundation rather
            than recreate it.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section records-section">
    <div class="site-container section-lead-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Beyond the code</span>
        <h2>The public core needs institutional infrastructure too.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="reading">
        <p class="section-intro">
          We maintain public governance, documentation standards, contribution
          rules, security reporting, and identity boundaries around the software
          so the surrounding system can evolve deliberately as the code does.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
